ell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186207483 :answer/value "| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $0$ | $20$ |\n| $4$ | $12$ |\n| $8$ | $20$ |" "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186208304 :question/worked-solution "To write the table, substitute each $x$ into\n\n$$\nf(x) = 6x - 1\n$$\n\nFor $x = -1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-1) &= 6(-1) - 1 \\\\\n&=-6 - 1 \\\\\n&=-7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x = 1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(1) &= 6(1) - 1 \\\\\n&= 6 - 1 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x = 2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(2) &= 6(2) - 1 \\\\\n&= 12 - 1 \\\\\n&= 11\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the table is the following:\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $-1$ | $-7$ |\n| $1$ | $5$ |\n| $2$ | $11$ |" "To write the table, substitute each $x$ into\n\n$$\nf(x) = 6x - 1\n$$\n\nFor $x = -1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-1) &= 6(-1) - 1 \\\\\n&=-6 - 1 \\\\\n&=-7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x = 1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(1) &= 6(1) - 1 \\\\\n&= 6 - 1 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x = 2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(2) &= 6(2) - 1 \\\\\n&= 12 - 1 \\\\\n&= 11\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the table is the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</th></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-7$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186208305 :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we can see that the points $(-3, 2)$, $(0, -4)$, and $(-2, 0)$ lie on the line.\n\nNow, we’ll analyze each of these points in turn:\n\n- For $(-3, 2)$: when $x = -3$, the corresponding $y$-value is $2$.\n- For $(0, -4)$: when $x = 0$, the corresponding $y$-value is $-4$.\n- For $(-2, 0)$: when $x = -2$, the corresponding $y$-value is $0$.\n\nTherefore, the table is:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $-3$ | $2$ |\n| $-2$ | $0$ |\n| $0$ | $-4$ |" "From the graph, we can see that the points $(-3, 2)$, $(0, -4)$, and $(-2, 0)$ lie on the line.\n\nNow, we’ll analyze each of these points in turn:\n\n- For $(-3, 2)$: when $x = -3$, the corresponding $y$-value is $2$.\n- For $(0, -4)$: when $x = 0$, the corresponding $y$-value is $-4$.\n- For $(-2, 0)$: when $x = -2$, the corresponding $y$-value is $0$.\n\nTherefore, the table is:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186208306 :question/worked-solution "The function\n\n$$\nf(x) = 15\n$$\n\nis a linear function where the output is always $15$ for any value of $x$.\nThat means every point on the graph has a $y$-coordinate of $15$.\n\nNow, we’ll analyze each of the given values of $x$ in turn:\n\n- For $x = 0$, we have $f(0) = 15$.\n- For $x = 1$, we have $f(1) = 15$.\n- For $x = 2$, we have $f(2) = 15$.\n\nTherefore, the table is\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $0$ | $15$ |\n| $1$ | $15$ |\n| $2$ | $15$ |" "The function\n\n$$\nf(x) = 15\n$$\n\nis a linear function where the output is always $15$ for any value of $x$.\nThat means every point on the graph has a $y$-coordinate of $15$.\n\nNow, we’ll analyze each of the given values of $x$ in turn:\n\n- For $x = 0$, we have $f(0) = 15$.\n- For $x = 1$, we have $f(1) = 15$.\n- For $x = 2$, we have $f(2) = 15$.\n\nTherefore, the table is\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186208307 :question/worked-solution "To write the table, we first express $y$ as a function of $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{4}y &= -5 - \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4}{3}(-5 - \\frac{1}{2}x) \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we’ll analyze each of the given values of $x$ in turn.\n\n- Consider $x = 0$.\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|=-\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}(0); =-\\frac{20}{3}\n$$\n- Consider $x = 3$.\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|=-\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}(3); =-\\frac{20}{3} - 2; =-\\frac{26}{3}\n$$\n- Consider $x = 6$.\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|=-\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}(6); =-\\frac{20}{3} - 4; =-\\frac{32}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the table is the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $0$ | $\\displaystyle -\\dfrac{20}{3}$ |\n| $3$ | $\\displaystyle -\\dfrac{26}{3}$ |\n| $6$ | $\\displaystyle -\\dfrac{32}{3}$ |" "To write the table, we first express $y$ as a function of $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{4}y &= -5 - \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4}{3}(-5 - \\frac{1}{2}x) \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we’ll analyze each of the given values of $x$ in turn.\n\n- Consider $x = 0$.\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|=-\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}(0); =-\\frac{20}{3}\n$$\n- Consider $x = 3$.\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|=-\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}(3); =-\\frac{20}{3} - 2; =-\\frac{26}{3}\n$$\n- Consider $x = 6$.\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|=-\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}(6); =-\\frac{20}{3} - 4; =-\\frac{32}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the table is the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\displaystyle -\\dfrac{20}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\displaystyle -\\dfrac{26}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\displaystyle -\\dfrac{32}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186208372 :question/problem "The high temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit $(^{\\circ}\\, \\mathrm{F})$, in a certain town was recorded for each of $5$ days.\n\n| Day | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| High temperature | $78$ | $77$ | $77$ | $78$ | $79$ |\n\nOver this $5$-day period, which of the following is **not** equal to $78^\\circ \\,\\mathrm{F}$ rounded to the nearest integer?\n\n1. Range of high temperatures\n2. Mean of the high temperatures\n3. Mode of the high temperatures\n4. Median of the high temperatures\n5. None of the listed" "The high temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit $(^{\\circ}\\, \\mathrm{F})$, in a certain town was recorded for each of $5$ days.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Day</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">High temperature</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$78$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$77$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$77$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$78$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$79$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nOver this $5$-day period, which of the following is **not** equal to $78^\\circ \\,\\mathrm{F}$ rounded to the nearest integer?\n\n1. Range of high temperatures\n2. Mean of the high temperatures\n3. Mode of the high temperatures\n4. Median of the high temperatures\n5. None of the listed"] [:db/cas 17592186208373 :question/problem "| Vendor | Items Sold |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Angela | $12$ |\n| Ben | $18$ |\n| Carlos | $15$ |\n| Dina | $21$ |\n| Ella | $16$ |\n| Fred | $17$ |\n\nThe table below shows the number of items sold by six market vendors on a single day in $2023$. Based on the table, what is the mean number of items sold by these $6$ vendors? Round your answer to the nearest integer." "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Vendor</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Items Sold</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Angela</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Ben</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$18$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Carlos</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Dina</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$21$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Ella</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$16$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Fred</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$17$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table below shows the number of items sold by six market vendors on a single day in $2023$. Based on the table, what is the mean number of items sold by these $6$ vendors? Round your answer to the nearest integer."] [:db/cas 17592186208374 :question/problem "| Day $1$ | Day $2$ | Day $3$ | Day $4$ | Day $5$ | Day $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $2.5$ | $3.1$ | $2.8$ | $2.8$ | $3.0$ | $3.5$ |\n\nThe table above shows the number of gallons of water consumed by a household on six different days. What is the median number of gallons consumed?" "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Day $1$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Day $2$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Day $3$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Day $4$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Day $5$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Day $6$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2.5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3.1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2.8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2.8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3.0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows the number of gallons of water consumed by a household on six different days. What is the median number of gallons consumed?"] [:db/cas 17592186208375 :question/problem "| Factory | Number of units produced in a day |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Alpha | $620$ |\n| Beta | $615$ |\n| Gamma | $612$ |\n| Delta | $630$ |\n| Epsilon | $618$ |\n\nA quality assurance team reviewed the number of units produced at several factories in one day. The median number of units produced across all sites reviewed was $620$. What is the difference between the median number of units produced for the $5$ factories listed above and the site-wide median?" "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Factory</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Number of units produced in a day</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Alpha</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$620$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Beta</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$615$<