rom the games played, what is the probability that it is a game of checkers?"] [:db/cas 17592186208381 :question/problem "Each of the $40$ pets at a shelter was classified as either dog, cat, or rabbit, as shown in the frequency table.\n\n| Pet Type | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Dog | $21$ |\n| Cat | $14$ |\n| Rabbit | $5$ |\n\nIf one of these pets is selected at random, what is the probability of selecting a rabbit?" "Each of the $40$ pets at a shelter was classified as either dog, cat, or rabbit, as shown in the frequency table.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Pet Type</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Dog</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$21$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Cat</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Rabbit</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nIf one of these pets is selected at random, what is the probability of selecting a rabbit?"] [:db/cas 17592186208382 :question/problem "| Age Group | Number of Members |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $0{-}9$ | $4$ |\n| $10{-}19$ | $6$ |\n| $20{-}29$ | $9$ |\n| $30{-}39$ | $10$ |\n| $40{-}49$ | $7$ |\n| $50{-}59$ | $3$ |\n\nThe table above shows how many members of a community fall within each age group. Of those members who are at least $20$ years old, what fraction are at least $40$ years old?" "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Age Group</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Number of Members</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0{-}9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10{-}19$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20{-}29$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30{-}39$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$40{-}49$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$50{-}59$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows how many members of a community fall within each age group. Of those members who are at least $20$ years old, what fraction are at least $40$ years old?"] [:db/cas 17592186208406 :question/problem "The function $z$ is defined by $z(x)=x^{2}+5$. Complete the following table for the values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $z(x)$?\n\n| $x$ | $z(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1$ |  |\n| $4$ |  |\n| $5$ |  |" "The function $z$ is defined by $z(x)=x^{2}+5$. Complete the following table for the values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $z(x)$?\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z(x)$</th></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186208406 :question/worked-solution "To determine the correct table, we calculate $z(x)$ for each of the given values of $x$.\n\n- For $x=1$, we get\n$$\n\\displaystyle z(1)|= 1^{2} + 5; = 1 + 5; = 6.\n$$\n- For $x=4$, we get\n$$\n\\displaystyle z(4)|= 4^{2} + 5; = 16 + 5; = 21.\n$$\n- For $x=5$, we get\n$$\n\\displaystyle z(5)|= 5^{2} + 5; = 25 + 5; = 30.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct table is the following.\n\n| $x$ | $z(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1$ | $6$ |\n| $4$ | $21$ |\n| $5$ | $30$ |" "To determine the correct table, we calculate $z(x)$ for each of the given values of $x$.\n\n- For $x=1$, we get\n$$\n\\displaystyle z(1)|= 1^{2} + 5; = 1 + 5; = 6.\n$$\n- For $x=4$, we get\n$$\n\\displaystyle z(4)|= 4^{2} + 5; = 16 + 5; = 21.\n$$\n- For $x=5$, we get\n$$\n\\displaystyle z(5)|= 5^{2} + 5; = 25 + 5; = 30.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct table is the following.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$21$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186208431 :question/problem "Consider the following inequality:\n\n$3x + 2y < 100$\n\nWhich of the following tables contains only points $(x, y)$ that satisfy this inequality?\n\nI\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $10$ | $20$ |\n| $15$ | $15$ |\n| $30$ | $20$ |\n\nII\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $5$ | $20$ |\n| $10$ | $15$ |\n| $30$ | $20$ |\n\nIII\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $10$ | $20$ |\n| $15$ | $10$ |\n| $5$ | $25$ |\n\nIV\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $15$ | $30$ |\n| $10$ | $25$ |\n| $20$ | $20$ |" "Consider the following inequality:\n\n$3x + 2y < 100$\n\nWhich of the following tables contains only points $(x, y)$ that satisfy this inequality?\n\nI\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"left\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nII\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"left\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nIII\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"left\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$25$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nIV\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"left\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$25$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186208431 :question/worked-solution "We are asked to determine which table contains only points $(x, y)$ that satisfy the inequality $3x + 2y < 100$. To do this, we substitute each point into the inequality and check whether it holds.\n\nNotice that for the points $(10, 20)$, $(15, 10)$, and $(5, 25)$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3(10) + 2(20) &= 30 + 40 = 70 < 100✓ \\\\\n3(15) + 2(10) &= 45 + 20 = 65 < 100✓ \\\\\n3(5) + 2(25) &= 15 + 50 = 65 < 100✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct table is the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $10$ | $20$ |\n| $15$ | $10$ |\n| $5$ | $25$ |" "We are asked to determine which table contains only points $(x, y)$ that satisfy the inequality $3x + 2y < 100$. To do this, we substitute each point into the inequality and check whether it holds.\n\nNotice that for the points $(10, 20)$, $(15, 10)$, and $(5, 25)$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3(10) + 2(20) &= 30 + 40 = 70 < 100✓ \\\\\n3(15) + 2(10) &= 45 + 20 = 65 < 100✓ \\\\\n3(5) + 2(25) &= 15 + 50 = 65 < 100✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct table is the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$25$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [:db/cas 17592186208456 :question/problem "The table below summarizes the number of restaurants that offer outdoor seating and provide free Wi-Fi.\n\n|  | Provides free Wi-Fi | Does not provide free Wi-Fi |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Has outdoor seating | $16$ | $4$ |\n| Does not have outdoor seating | $11$ | $9$ |\n\nIf one of these restaurants is selected at random, what is the probability that it **has outdoor seating but does not provide free Wi-Fi**?" "The table below summarizes the number of restaurants that offer outdoor seating and provide free Wi-Fi.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Provides free Wi-Fi</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Does not provide free Wi-Fi</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Has outdoor seating</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Does not have outdoor seating</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nIf one of these restaurants is selected at random, what is the probability that it **has outdoor seating but does not provide free Wi-Fi**?"] [:db/cas 17592186208456 :question/worked-solution "To determine the desired probability, we must find the ratio of the number of restaurants that have outdoor seating but do not provide free Wi-Fi to the total number of restaurants.\n\nWe can see from the table that there are a total of\n\n$$\n16 + 4 + 11 + 9 = {\\color{red}40}\n$$\n\nrestaurants. Of this amount, ${\\color{blue}4}$ have outdoor seating but do not provide free Wi-Fi.\n\n|  | Provides free Wi-Fi | Does not provide free Wi-Fi |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Has outdoor seating | $16$ | $\\color{blue}4$ |\n| Does not have outdoor seating | $11$ | $9$ |\n\nTherefore, the desired probability is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle P ( \\text{Outdoor seating but no Wi-Fi} ) & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{ {\\color{blue}4}}{ {\\color{red}40}}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{1 \\cdot  4}{10 \\cdot  4}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{1 \\cdot  \\cancel{4}}{10 \\cdot  \\cancel{4}}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{10}} .\\end{array}}\n$$" "To determine the desired probability, we must find the ratio of the number of restaurants that have outdoor seating but do not provide free Wi-Fi to the total number of restaurants.\n\nWe can see from the table that there are a total of\n\n$$\n16 + 4 + 11 + 9 = {\\color{red}40}\n$$\n\nrestaurants. Of this amount, ${\\color{blue}4}$ have outdoor seating but do not provide free Wi-Fi.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Provides free Wi-Fi</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Does not provide free Wi-Fi</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Has outdoor seating</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFF8E5\">$\\color{blue}4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Does not have outdoor seating</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, the desired probability is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle P ( \\text{Outdoor seating but no Wi-Fi} ) & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{ {\\color{blue}4}}{ {\\color{red}40}}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{1 \\cdot  4}{10 \\cdot  4}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{1 \\cdot  \\cancel{4}}{10 \\cdot  \\cancel{4}}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{10}} .\\end{array}}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186208458 :question/problem "The table below shows the distribution of different types of donations collected in three neighborhoods for $100$ donations.\n\n| Donation | North | South | East | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Food | $8$ | $10$ | $12$ | $30$ |\n| Clothes | $9$ | $11$ | $10$ | $30$ |\n| Books | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $24$ |\n| Toys | $6$ | $5$ | $5$ | $16$ |\n| **Total** | **$30$** | **$34$** | **$36$** | **$100$** |\n\nIf one donation is selected at random, what is the probability that it was a Books donation?" "The table below shows the distribution of different types of donations collected in three neighborhoods for $100$ donations.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Donation</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">North</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">South</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">East</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Total</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Food</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Clothes</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Books</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$24$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Toys</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$30$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$34$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$36$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$100$</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nIf one donation is selected at random, what is the probability that it was a Books donation?"] [:db/cas 17592186208458 :question/worked-solution "To determine the desired probability, we must find the ratio of the number of Books donations to the total number of donations.\n\nWe are told that there were $100$ total donations, of which ${\\color{blue}24}$ were Books.\n\n| Donation | North | South | East | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Food | $8$ | $10$ | $12$ | $30$ |\n| Clothes | $9$ | $11$ | $10$ | $30$ |\n| Books | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $\\color{blue}24$ |\n| Toys | $6$ | $5$ | $5$ | $16$ |\n| **Total** | **$30$** | **$34$** | **$36$** | **$100$** |\n\nTherefore, the desired probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(\\text{Books}) = \\dfrac{\\color{blue}24}{100} = \\dfrac{6}{25}\n$$" "To determine the desired probability, we must find the ratio of the number of Books donations to the total number of donations.\n\nWe are told that there were $100$ total donations, of which ${\\color{blue}24}$ were Books.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Donation</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">North</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">South</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">East</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Total</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Food</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Clothes</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Books</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFF8E5\">$\\color{blue}24$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Toys</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$30$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$34$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$36$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$100$</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, the desired probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(\\text{Books}) = \\dfrac{\\color{blue}24}{100} = \\dfrac{6}{25}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186208459 :question/problem "|  | Shoes purchased | Shoes not purchased | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Jersey purchased | $80$ | $40$ | $120$ |\n| Jersey not purchased | $30$ | $50$ | $80$ |\n| **Total** | **$110$** | **$90$** | **$200$** |\n\nIn a weekend, a sports shop had a total of $200$ customers. The table above summarizes whether or not customers bought a jersey, shoes, both, or neither. Based on the data in the table, what is the probability that a randomly selected customer did not purchase a jersey?" "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Shoes purchased</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Shoes not purchased</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Total</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Jersey purchased</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$80$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$40$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$120$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Jersey not purchased</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$50$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$80$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$110$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$90$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$200$</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nIn a weekend, a sports shop had a total of $200$ customers. The table above summarizes whether or not customers bought a jersey, shoes, both, or neither. Based on the data in the table, what is the probability that a randomly selected customer did not purchase a jersey?"] [:db/cas 17592186208459 :question/worked-solution "To determine the desired probability, we must find the ratio of the number of customers who did not purchase a jersey to the number of people who visited the sports shop on Sunday.\n\nWe are told that the shop had $200$ customers on that particular Sunday. Of this amount, ${\\color{blue}80}$ did not purchase a jersey.\n\n|  | Shoes purchased | Shoes not purchased | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Jersey purchased | $80$ | $40$ | $120$ |\n| Jersey not purchased | $30$ | $50$ | $\\color{blue}80$ |\n| **Total** | **$110$** | **$90$** | **$200$** |\n\nTherefore, the desired probability is given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle P ( \\text{Jersey not purchased} ) & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{ {\\color{blue}80}}{200}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{2 \\cdot  40}{5 \\cdot  40}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{2 \\cdot  \\cancel{40}}{5 \\cdot  \\cancel{40}}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{2}{5}} .\\end{array}}\n$$" "To determine the desired probability, we must find the ratio of the number of customers who did not purchase a jersey to the number of people who visited the sports shop on Sunday.\n\nWe are told that the shop had $200$ customers on that particular Sunday. Of this amount, ${\\color{blue}80}$ did not purchase a jersey.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Shoes purchased</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Shoes not purchased</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Total</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Jersey purchased</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$80$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$40$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$120$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Jersey not purchased</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$50$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFF8E5\">$\\color{blue}80$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$110$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$90$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$200$</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, the desired probability is given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle P ( \\text{Jersey not purchased} ) & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{ {\\color{blue}80}}{200}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{2 \\cdot  40}{5 \\cdot  40}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{2 \\cdot  \\cancel{40}}{5 \\cdot  \\cancel{40}}} \\\\ \\displaystyle  & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{2}{5}} .\\end{array}}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186208463 :question/problem "A company randomly sampled $500$ employees about a proposed remote–work policy. The results were categorized by department and are shown below.\n\n|  | Plan to vote<br>for<br>Plan A | Plan to vote<br>for<br>Plan B |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Tech | 