nter\">$101.7$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$108.3$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Country H</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$95.9$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$97.8$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Country I</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$140.8$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$150.0$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nBased on the information in the table, how much greater, in terawatt-hours, was the median electricity generation in $2005$ than in $2001$, rounded to the nearest tenth of a terawatt-hour?\n\nThe median electricity generation in $2005$ was $\\boxed{ {\\phantom{X X X X X}}}$ terawatt-hours greater than in $2001$."] [:db/cas 17592186208478 :question/problem "The table shows the streaming bitrates, rounded to the nearest whole number, for a group of $57$ video sessions.\n\n| Bitrate | Number of Sessions |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $4$ | $6$ |\n| $5$ | $7$ |\n| $6$ | $8$ |\n| $7$ | $8$ |\n| $8$ | $10$ |\n| $9$ | $9$ |\n| $10$ | $9$ |\n\nA new bitrate of $20$ is added to the dataset, making $58$ bitrates in total. Which of the following statements best compares the mean and median of the new dataset to those of the original dataset?\n\n1. The mean of the new dataset is less than the mean of the original dataset, and the medians of the two datasets are equal.\n2. The mean of the new dataset is greater than the mean of the original dataset, and the medians of the two datasets are equal.\n3. The mean of the new dataset is less than the mean of the original dataset, and the median of the new dataset is less than the median of the original dataset.\n4. The mean of the new dataset is greater than the mean of the original dataset, and the median of the new dataset is greater than the median of the original dataset.\n5. The mean of the new dataset is greater than the mean of the original dataset, and the median of the new dataset is less than the median of the original dataset." "The table s