6$ | $72$ | $70$ | $71$ |\n\nWhat was the mean low temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit, during the five-day period?" "The table below displays the high and low temperatures in Miami, Florida, over a five-day period.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\"></th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Monday</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Tuesday</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Wednesday</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Thursday</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\">Friday</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">High temperature</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$88$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$91$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$86$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$89$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$90$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">Low temperature</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$74$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$76$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$72$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$70$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$71$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nWhat was the mean low temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit, during the five-day period?"] [:db/cas 17592186209094 :question/problem "The high temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit $(^{∘}F)$, in a certain town was recorded for each of $5$ days.\n\n| Day | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| High temperature | $78$ | $77$ | $77$ | $78$ | $79$ |\n\nOver this $5$-day period, which of the following is **not** equal to $78^{∘}F$ rounded to the nearest integer?" "The high temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit $(^{∘}F)$, in a certain town was recorded for each of $5$ days.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-alig