ds.\n\n| Orchard | Number of Oranges |\n| --- | ---: |\n| A | $120$ |\n| B | $135$ |\n| C | $142$ |\n| D | $128$ |\n| E | $140$ |\n| F | $130$ |\n\nA seventh orchard produced $150$ oranges, and this value is added to the original dataset of six orchards to create a new dataset. Which statement correctly compares the means of the two datasets?" "The table shows the number of oranges harvested from six orchards.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Orchard</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Number of Oranges</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">A</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$120$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">B</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$135$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">C</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$142$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">D</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$128$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">E</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$140$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">F</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$130$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nA seventh orchard produced $150$ oranges, and this value is added to the original dataset of six orchards to create a new dataset. Which statement correctly compares the means of the two datasets?"] [:db/cas 17592186209460 :question/problem "The table shows heart rates (beats per minute) measured at six time intervals during a workout.\n\n| Interval | Heart Rate (bpm) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 1 | $120$ |\n| 2 | $125$ |\n| 3 | $118$ |\n| 4 | $122$ |\n| 5 | $127$ |\n| 6 | $121$ |\n\nA seventh interval measured $140$ bpm, and this value is added 